From 9b7baf3089624d85466497e97373bcde5d79f4be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:06:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Runner: the results' menu is each player's own (Restart, Back
 to Menu)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Gibax (2026-11-26): "le menu qui suit, on empêche de sélectionner replay
(atm), mais restart te renvoie dans l'écran d'attente du runner (pour
relancer la course, en attendant que tout le monde revienne ou non) ;
sélectionner return to menu te renvoie au menu, et te déconnecte du reste";
"c'est à chaque runner de choisir son option".

The results' menu is the task 0x80528C9C (found in RAM dumps): state +20
(4: open), cursor +22 (Restart, Replay, Back to Menu), kind +28 (0); it
opens at the same frame on every machine. There each runner leaves the
lockstep (END to the relay) and its own player drives its menu:
- the menus read the players' controller structures (0x8040BC60, from racer
  0, a player's only); racer 0 points to port 0's, as in a 1P game;
- A on Replay is dropped;
- A on Restart is kept from the game: AGAIN to the relay, the race ended by
  the runner (EndRace: its code words back before a state is loaded over
  them), the waiting screen until GO, the start state loaded again, the
  lockstep from frame 1; the waiting screen stays until the race loads;
- A on Back to Menu goes to the game; the race's manager (0x80434414) only
  acts on the choice in its state 9 (0x80435D44), which it reaches when a
  player of the game has finished ([0x806129B5]), never with the seats'
  racers as CPUs: this machine's manager goes to 9; then the race ends,
  BYE, the runner leaves the relay, and the game is in its own menus.
SRNP_FIN_CHOIX=restart|menu|replay: the choice for tests.

Measured, 3 runners (Tails, Jet, Wave, all AI): Tails Restart, Jet Back to
Menu (the game's Normal Race menu, alone), Wave Replay (dropped) then
Restart; the second race with Tails and Wave, Jet's racer to the AI;
128 identical checksums over both races, 0 divergences.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
